# Host binaries: no extension, so the root .gitignore's *.elf rule misses them.
actionfuzz
actiontest
bittest
imgtest
mkswf
ppmcheck
ppmcmp
swfdump
sndtest
swfcost
ramptest
swffuzz
swffuzz-san
swfrender
swftrace
tricmp

# Everything `make check` produces. The .swf files in here are generated by
# mkswf and are reproducible in milliseconds; the .ppm files are renders.
#
# This also keeps renders of real-world .swf files out of the repository,
# which matters beyond tidiness: the file this was developed against is a Sega
# intro. Using it locally to check interoperability is fine, redistributing it
# or pictures of it is not.
out/
*.ppm

# The same rule for a .swf dropped anywhere in this directory rather than only
# in out/. corpus.sh fetches third-party files to a temporary directory and
# never copies one here, but the rule that keeps somebody else's content out of
# the history should not depend on a script continuing to be careful - and out/
# alone did not say that.
*.swf
